      "text": "Experiments performed on Chinese Facebook data and English online debate forum data show that UTCNN achieves a 0.755 macro-average f-score for supportive, neutral, and unsupportive stance classes on Facebook data, which is significantly better than models in which either user, topic, or comment information is withheld.\n\n2.\n\nIn the Facebook dataset we study, we use comments instead of reply links.\n\nThey show\n\nFBFans is a privately-owned, single-topic, Chinese, unbalanced, social media dataset, and CreateDebate is a public, multiple-topic, English, balanced, forum dataset.\n\nThe FBFans dataset contains data from anti-nuclear-power Chinese Facebook fan groups from September 2013 to August 2014, including posts and their author and liker IDs.\n\nThere are a total of\n\nThe CreateDebate dataset was collected from an English online debate forum discussing four topics: abortion (ABO), gay rights (GAY), Obama (OBA), and marijuana (MAR).\n\nAll user and topic embeddings were randomly initialized in the range of [-0.1 0.1].\n\nFor the CreateDebate dataset, which itself constitutes four topics, the topic labels for posts were used directly without additionally applying LDA.\n\nFor the",
